WEBVTT

1
00:00:00.600 --> 00:00:11.130
Hi! A box holds 10 pencils. 4 boxes and 7 more: how many? Today we'll learn numbers up to 100.

2
00:00:11.280 --> 00:00:13.962
10 ones make 1 ten.

3
00:00:14.112 --> 00:00:19.818
Count in tens: 10, 20, 30, all the way to 100.

4
00:00:19.968 --> 00:00:22.650
10 tens make 100.

5
00:00:22.800 --> 00:00:27.762
4 tens and 7 ones make 47.

6
00:00:27.912 --> 00:00:32.898
In 47, the tens digit is 4 and the ones digit is 7.

7
00:00:33.048 --> 00:00:37.794
To compare, look at the tens first: more tens means bigger.

8
00:00:37.944 --> 00:00:41.274
If the tens are the same, compare the ones.

9
00:00:41.424 --> 00:00:50.562
63 is greater than 58 because 6 tens beat 5 tens; 45 is less than 49.

10
00:00:50.712 --> 00:00:54.378
Watch out! Don't look at the ones first!

11
00:00:54.528 --> 00:00:59.514
38 has only 3 tens; 52 has 5 tens.

12
00:00:59.664 --> 00:01:04.338
So 38 is less than 52.

13
00:01:04.488 --> 00:01:13.242
Your turn! What number is 6 tens and 2 ones? Pause and think.

14
00:01:13.392 --> 00:01:20.322
6 tens is 60, plus 2 is 62. Did you get it right?

15
00:01:20.472 --> 00:01:29.010
Another one! What is the tens digit of 85? Pause and think.

16
00:01:29.160 --> 00:01:35.106
The tens digit of 85 is 8. Did you get it right?

17
00:01:35.256 --> 00:01:44.490
Here's another! Which is greater, 70 or 69? Pause and think.

18
00:01:44.640 --> 00:01:51.570
7 tens beat 6 tens, so 70 is greater. Did you get it right?

19
00:01:51.720 --> 00:02:01.170
Try one more! Which is greater, 54 or 57? Pause and think.

20
00:02:01.320 --> 00:02:08.922
Same tens, 7 is more than 4, so 57 is greater. Did you get it right?

21
00:02:09.072 --> 00:02:17.658
Try one more! What number comes after 99? Pause and think.

22
00:02:17.808 --> 00:02:23.706
One more than 99 is 100. Did you get it right?

23
00:02:23.856 --> 00:02:32.226
Try one more! 30, 40, what, 60? Pause and think.

24
00:02:32.376 --> 00:02:37.794
Counting in tens, it's 50. Did you get it right?

25
00:02:37.944 --> 00:02:49.314
Last one! Put 72, 27 and 45 in order from smallest to biggest. Pause and think.

26
00:02:49.464 --> 00:02:59.370
Compare tens: 2, 4, 7, so 27, 45, 72. Did you get it right?

27
00:02:59.520 --> 00:03:06.162
Remember: a 2-digit number is tens and ones. Compare the tens first, then the ones.

28
00:03:06.312 --> 00:03:11.826
Find house numbers or page numbers at home and read them!

